From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gareth Davidson <gareth@aros.org>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] IPrefs: avoid Workbench reset requester during startup

Upstream AROS e92efb9ee4, imported verbatim. Our pin d0370bd757 predates it.

Loading the initial font preferences can attempt to close the Workbench screen
while the startup Shell still has an open window. If CloseWorkBench fails,
IPrefs puts up a Retry/Cancel requester and stops applying the rest of the
preferences -- on a machine nobody is sitting at, that is a stall with no way
out.

Marks only the initial notification batch as an initial load and cancels the
screen reset without a requester during that phase; the normal requester stays
for live preference changes afterwards.

This is the other end of 0015, and does not apply to the pinned tree without
it -- 0015 reshapes main.c first. Numeric order in this series is therefore
load-bearing, which it already was.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/workbench/c/iprefs/fontprefs.c b/workbench/c/iprefs/fontprefs.c
index f2a84230ad..750805fd30 100644
--- a/workbench/c/iprefs/fontprefs.c
+++ b/workbench/c/iprefs/fontprefs.c
@@ -129,12 +129,23 @@ void FontPrefs_Handler(STRPTR filename)
                                 {
                                     closed = CloseWorkBench();
                                     if (!closed)
-                                        cancel = ShowMessage("System Request",
-                                            "Intuition is attempting to reset"
-                                            " the Workbench Screen.\n"
-                                            "Please close all windows,"
-                                            " except drawers.",
-                                            "Retry|Cancel") == 0;
+                                    {
+                                        /* An initial preference load can run
+                                         * while the startup Shell still prevents
+                                         * CloseWorkBench(). Do not wedge IPrefs
+                                         * in an unanswerable requester and leave
+                                         * later preferences unapplied. Live
+                                         * changes retain the normal requester. */
+                                        if (initial_load)
+                                            cancel = TRUE;
+                                        else
+                                            cancel = ShowMessage("System Request",
+                                                "Intuition is attempting to reset"
+                                                " the Workbench Screen.\n"
+                                                "Please close all windows,"
+                                                " except drawers.",
+                                                "Retry|Cancel") == 0;
+                                    }
                                 }
                                 if (closed)
                                     OpenWorkBench();
diff --git a/workbench/c/iprefs/main.c b/workbench/c/iprefs/main.c
index 84e1de037a..ed49d93eac 100644
--- a/workbench/c/iprefs/main.c
+++ b/workbench/c/iprefs/main.c
@@ -361,7 +361,9 @@ int main(void)
 
     Detach();  // No more console I/O beyond this point.
 
+    initial_load = TRUE;
     HandleNotify();
+    initial_load = FALSE;
     HandleAll();
     Cleanup(NULL);
 
@@ -369,5 +371,3 @@ int main(void)
 }
 
 /*********************************************************************************************/
-
-
diff --git a/workbench/c/iprefs/vars.h b/workbench/c/iprefs/vars.h
index 276a7b51fa..1d78fe477f 100644
--- a/workbench/c/iprefs/vars.h
+++ b/workbench/c/iprefs/vars.h
@@ -47,3 +47,4 @@ VAR UBYTE   	    	    	pointerprefsname[256];
 VAR UBYTE   	    	    	overscanprefsname[256];
 
 VAR BOOL    	    	    	patches_installed;
+VAR BOOL    	    	    	initial_load;
